{"title":"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Testing_Pythagorean_Triples)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Testing Pythagorean Triples)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TechMath_Thinker\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TechMath Thinker</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_🚀_2_min_solve_🚀\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 🚀 2 min solve 🚀</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#VIdeo_Solution_2_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">VIdeo Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a rectangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d673e7bfd3b23e5b1e42d80e530215b230057a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 30$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5188fc52c0abb471c46b4b2283321afa68262a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> respectively so that all sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/46967ae50c32047d5674d1506c5b18abd0ca3fb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABP}, \\triangle{PCQ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac0bd0d72aa17afe1d3cf509a4ed1ed1dba3bc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{QDA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> have integer lengths. What is the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6803188da30bd86a35e531f3213a582cef94e927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{APQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d7967b1766cf3de4f0c1d0e4dfee1d23c91ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 84 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 86 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 88 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 90 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Testing_Pythagorean_Triples.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Testing_Pythagorean_Triples)\">Solution 1 (Testing Pythagorean Triples)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Testing Pythagorean Triples)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fc6aee278a2183fa354f7d7f71a911b18f7b29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* ~ItsMeNoobieboy */ size(200); pair A, B, C, D, P, Q; A = (0,28/30); B = (1,28/30); C = (1,0); D = (0,0); P = (1,12/30); Q = (21/30,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--P--Q--cycle); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,E,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S,linewidth(4)); label(&quot;$30$&quot;,midpoint(A--B),N); label(&quot;$16$&quot;,midpoint(B--P),E); label(&quot;$34$&quot;,midpoint(A--P),NE, red); label(&quot;$28$&quot;,midpoint(A--D),W); label(&quot;$21$&quot;,midpoint(D--Q),S); label(&quot;$35$&quot;,midpoint(A--Q),SW, red); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(Q--C),S); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,midpoint(C--P),E); label(&quot;$15$&quot;,midpoint(Q--P),SE, red); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"308\" />\n</p><p>We know that all side lengths are integers, so we can test Pythagorean triples for all triangles. \n</p><p>First, we focus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e21688b2f6b32cf5f441880b86d52c10c21a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABP}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the possible (small enough) Pythagorean triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e21688b2f6b32cf5f441880b86d52c10c21a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABP}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> can be are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71a9fa1de4f6b06c8af59f0ac39708cd9a008fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4, 5), (5, 12, 13), (8, 15, 17),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"232\" height=\"20\" /> where the length of the longer leg is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Testing these, we get that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138e3c954652e8e96153c1e75b1bbdc0355579a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8, 15, 17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> is a valid solution. Thus, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3b12da0121d07ed3598f5b27a5cacf62a2f75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd67a343a80211c6198b7b5bcb64943f251ab36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Next, we move on to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac0bd0d72aa17afe1d3cf509a4ed1ed1dba3bc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{QDA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the small enough triples are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b168b4f593e84efc74ec9309f133365d8a0b4c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf204f5bffc555354bd2ee5b35b8661ea2bb25bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7, 24, 25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. Testing again, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b168b4f593e84efc74ec9309f133365d8a0b4c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is our triple. We get the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0afab115f69a29c63e6694affe416fcf9e0f3d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/166fb8d3ee6310b719241e0c6312ff9e96c78b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ecd7c28e12e207bf48530ad23ff21de62197b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ = CD - DQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e27d40d4494f6a8134f09ea7a3f5302eb325ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP = BC - BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aadc3982602f720205c013502de0e7da613bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CPQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> is therefore a right triangle with side length ratios <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b09f89ef98d585c0f756347a629296459191da6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3, 4, 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, and the hypotenuse is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6803188da30bd86a35e531f3213a582cef94e927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{APQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106af38d3cd2dfed7b58381ed1620e7aade42be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34, 35,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b477ff41e1b4c1050d4dd41bcea08de66eb9eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> so the perimeter is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e99aade1a5d8b91cdbe41e752e3454f008b307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34 + 35 + 15 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 84}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"195\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Gabe Horn ~ItsMeNoobieboy ~oinava\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61fe5a375f4d8e40fb5c60f3475d07e0dd4a6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7aca7b0c2dd78f5ede29b8549ff17183fcf820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd1baad72680898dd19c38a5a7efc7367ecbee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{2}+y^{2}=z^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c99786e47b27e98eb5c555b6a7489d1138ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> on both sides, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/12260faf7fed5b5dec90762eefe49ccbcf25e047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{2}=z^{2}-y^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. Factoring, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/074714775faeb6911c5608eb02e9911dca9d7b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{2}=(z-y)(z+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are integers, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f1d516db531c1a66f4f54fec76743404a5c06b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955b0030c06d258b4b9a46188afd9c88bb91634c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> have to be even or both have to be odd. We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d023935cd257dfbd99d3f90766561c0d27a704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. We can pretty easily see now that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/6740b497195e460f077bec21e7c0507a650c7cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-y=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a765e1e8d0cd1c72bd69debafc1df7a3bd9f6eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+y=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf709e521fe3f0bae584d735bda8a7c0b5627984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de17c4b291b3093225ab316e404d77f09e296201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />. We now get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4509b6925686740fa911b8b854abbad75da00d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. We do the same trick again. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c2037faf7a214ef7d01093b44c510a4c4301e625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21feec53de89528e812ad4b39f94a2cfbc6c3d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9204246eedb581d9c0d09e68d3f84e49daa67196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28^{2}=(b+a)(b-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />. We can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/f/d3f604376125d0273f1c1507d57854aaf1729914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+a=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f9280a48aa06256b288b99cac46460223ed14d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/8449c3f59b30a296e1ef2c3b860b10ea2650f412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d2025bb35622bbd802d3d4eef27cc9dbd59be4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/304b0cd97668ab381c695bb351dbd62870635395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and by the Pythagorean Theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d55da056cbfeb644f364e290eb90be01e5b2721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5c7c23d3557dec453c0d45d798937844b01f5c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP+PQ+AQ=34+15+35=84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34abc576cd88073a7fef724ded0891fb5846e86f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 84}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"72\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>If you want to see a video solution on this solution, look at Video Solution 1.\n</p><p>-paixiao (minor edits-HW73)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TechMath_Thinker\">Video Solution by TechMath Thinker</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TechMath Thinker\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/64ZSavdZro0\">https://youtu.be/64ZSavdZro0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Little Fermat\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=FPZ1D4hdcd1QGUK2&amp;t=3834\">https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=FPZ1D4hdcd1QGUK2&amp;t=3834</a>\n~little-fermat\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=KfPIbpJjHwZQTyH4&amp;t=4479\">https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=KfPIbpJjHwZQTyH4&amp;t=4479</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.F0.9F.9A.80_2_min_solve_.F0.9F.9A.80\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_🚀_2_min_solve_🚀\">Video Solution 🚀 2 min solve 🚀</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 🚀 2 min solve 🚀\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HVMlhdSurPw\">https://youtu.be/HVMlhdSurPw</a>\n</p><p><i> ~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a 